4, 2, 1, Go!

So this is my very first blog post.
Actually, just a few hours ago, I did not know how it is going to start and
what I will be writing in it. However, it is a fortune that I came across a very nice package called Scikit-Learn which is at the same time, a library for machine learning, and a tutorial for pattern recognition. I have just finished a pattern recognition course at TU Delft as part of my training plan of the PhD program, I found it very fascinating, but didn't have time to put good effort in it. However, I do wish to acquire good knowledge of (applied) machine learning and pattern recognition so that I can feel comfortable when facing a problem, in prepration for my future carerr (if possible) to work more in data (science) analysis field, and if possible to help other people (probably students) who do not have good access to good material, or do not have experienced enough.

So my plan is that I will try to follow scikit learn and if needed write down my summary, may be in the form of recapitulation or a cheat sheet for later reference or newcomers of this field. For a disclaimer, I would like to say that all of the posts following are supposed to be from my understanding from the past and/or after reading/trying/studying. They are by no mean to be fully qualified or justified. All comments and feedbacks are welcomed as long as they are for constructive purpose and in constructive manners. Please stick to general communication etiquette. So if you found something confusing or may not sound right, please raise a discussion or consult with another expert. I would also love to hear from you. Remember I am also learning.

